\title{Case-insensitive equality}
\date{2026-03-07T23:50:58Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Example}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{We can define a relation on strings where two strings are related if they have the same characters in the same order, except that letters may differ in whether they are upper- or lowercase.  For example, \code{Straw!} would be related to \code{sTRaW!} but not to \code{strawberry}, nor to \code{warts}.}
